# Implementation Plan: Deploying IT Inventory to DeanOS

This plan outlines the steps to replace the current IT Inventory installation on the DeanOS server (`192.168.1.186`) with the updated "premium" version from the local workspace.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The deployment will involve restarting the `it-inventory` Docker container on the server. This will result in a brief downtime (approx. 30-60 seconds).
>
> [!WARNING]
> We will be syncing the `/DATA/dean/projects/My-Personal-Repository/` directory on the server. A full backup will be created before any changes are applied.

## Proposed Changes

### IT Inventory Deployment [DeanOS]

1.  **Preparation**:
    - [x] Verify local repository status (`C:\projects\it-inventory`).
    - [x] Identify deployment path on server: `/DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
2.  **Server Cleanup**:
    - [x] SSH into DeanOS (`192.168.1.186`).
    - [x] Remove existing container `it-inventory` (if any).
    - [x] Remove old project directory `/DATA/projects/it-inventory` (if any).
3.  **Fresh Deployment**:
    - [x] Clone the repository: `git clone https://github.com/evatechnosoft/My-Personal-Repository.git /DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
    - [x] Create `.env` from `.env.example` and configure `APP_BASE_URL`.
    - [x] Build and start the service: `sudo docker compose up -d --build app`.
    - [ ] Set final permissions: `sudo chown -R dean:samba /DATA/projects/it-inventory`.
4.  **Verification**:
    - [x] Check container logs: `sudo docker logs it-inventory`.
    - [ ] Confirm web access: `http://192.168.1.186:8001`.
    - [ ] Test UI buttons ("Add New Device", "Add Request").

---

### Phase 2: Coolify Installation & Configuration

1.  **Core Installation [DeanOS]**:
    - SSH into DeanOS.
    - Run official Coolify installation script: `curl -fsSL https://cdn.coollabs.io/coolify/install.sh | bash`.
    - Monitor progress and ensure Docker is managing the new containers (`coolify`, `coolify-realtime`, etc.).
2.  **SSH Infrastructure**:
    - Ensure the `coolify` user/container can access the host via the provided `coolos.pub` key if needed.
    - [ ] Update local `~/.ssh/config` with the `coolos` entry.
3.  **Access & Setup**:
    - Verify access at `http://192.168.1.186:8000`.
    - Guided setup for the first admin user.

